Chapter 7: The Human–AI Knowledge Balance

Future colonies are symbiotes of human and machine cognition. The balance is delicate.

Definition 7.1 (Human Autonomy Coefficient). Partition total knowledge into human and AI contributions:

H = \sum_{i \in V_H} \sum_s k_{is}, \qquad A = \sum_{i \in V_A} \sum_s k_{is}.
\]  

The human autonomy coefficient is

\alpha = \frac{H}{H + A}.

Theorem 7.1 (Comprehension Probability). If  \alpha < \alpha_{\text{critical}} , the probability that a randomly selected operational decision rests on knowledge that no human comprehends exceeds  1 - \alpha .
Proof. Under uniform sampling of all knowledge units in the colony, the fraction that is intelligible to at least one human equals  \alpha . The complement gives the probability of an opaque decision. ∎

When  \alpha  drops too low, humans become moral ornamentation on an autonomous machine civilization. We now determine the long‑run equilibrium of this coefficient under dynamic growth.

Theorem 7.2 (Asymptotic Human–AI Balance).
Assume human knowledge  H(t)  and AI knowledge  A(t)  evolve according to linear dynamics

\dot{H} = \gamma_H - \lambda_H H,\qquad \dot{A} = \gamma_A - \lambda_A A,
\]  

with positive growth rates  \gamma_H,\gamma_A  and decay constants  \lambda_H,\lambda_A>0 . Then

\lim_{t\to\infty}\alpha(t) = \frac{\gamma_H \lambda_A}{\gamma_H \lambda_A + \gamma_A \lambda_H}.
\]  

Consequently, the constraint  \alpha(t) > \alpha_{\text{critical}}  for all large  t  is equivalent to the design inequality

\frac{\gamma_H}{\lambda_H} > \frac{\alpha_{\text{critical}}}{1-\alpha_{\text{critical}}} \cdot \frac{\gamma_A}{\lambda_A}.
\]  

Proof. The ODEs are linear and decoupled. Their steady states are  H^* = \gamma_H/\lambda_H ,  A^* = \gamma_A/\lambda_A . The transient terms decay exponentially, so  \alpha(t) \to H^*/(H^*+A^*) . Substituting yields the limit expression. Solving  \alpha^* > \alpha_{\text{critical}}  gives the claimed inequality. ∎

The Cognitive Cartographer uses this relation to set bounds on the permissible growth of AI knowledge relative to human training pipelines, ensuring meaningful human oversight persists permanently.

