10.5 Stability Under Resource Fluctuations

The lunar environment is volatile. A power outage in the training lab, a delayed resupply of nutritional supplements—these perturb the total budget C_{\text{total}}. The Cartographer must know that the cognitive configuration will not unravel.

Lemma 10.5 (Sensitivity to Resource Fluctuation).
The optimal expertise allocation k_{is}^* is Lipschitz continuous in the total resource budget C_{\text{total}}. Small changes in available resources cause only proportionally small, predictable adjustments; there is no catastrophic churn.

Proof.
Let \mathbf{k}^*(\mu) be the optimum for shadow price \mu. The KKT system

\nabla_{\mathbf{k}} CI - \mu \nabla_{\mathbf{k}} \mathcal{C} = 0, \qquad \sum \mathcal{C}_{is}(k_{is}) = C_{\text{total}}
\]  

implicitly defines \mathbf{k}^* as a function of C_{\text{total}}. Differentiating with respect to the budget,

\begin{bmatrix}
\nabla^2 CI - \mu \nabla^2 \mathcal{C} & -\nabla_{\mathbf{k}} \mathcal{C} \\
-(\nabla_{\mathbf{k}} \mathcal{C})^\top & 0
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
d\mathbf{k}^* \\ d\mu
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0 \\ dC_{\text{total}}
\end{bmatrix}.
\]  

The upper‑left block is negative definite (since CI is concave and \mathcal{C} is convex, -\mu\nabla^2\mathcal{C} is negative semidefinite), and the whole bordered Hessian is non‑singular by strict complementary slackness. The Implicit Function Theorem then guarantees that d\mathbf{k}^*/dC_{\text{total}} exists and is bounded in norm, establishing Lipschitz continuity. ∎

Thus, a sudden 5% drop in training resources does not force the colony to drop a life‑critical skill below threshold; the Cartographer’s optimisation smoothly re‑scales efforts while preserving the Triplicate Rule and human autonomy constraints.

