10.6 Operational Implementation: The Marginal Efficiency of Cognition (MEC)

In practice, the Cartographer does not recalculate the full integral daily. The digital twin (Chapter 8) monitors the real‑time marginal costs c_{i,s} and the gradient \partial CI/\partial k_{is}. The Marginal Efficiency of Cognition (MEC) for each (individual, skill) pair is

MEC_{is} = \frac{1}{c_{i,s}} \frac{\partial CI}{\partial k_{is}}.
\]  

Training resources are reallocated hourly toward the pairs with the highest MEC, ensuring the colony’s cognitive “brain” is constantly tuned to its survival context.

