\]  

4. Substituting  u_{ij}^*  back yields the closed‑loop HJB equation. ∎

Interpretation for the Cartographer. The optimal intervention along a cognitive edge is proportional to the negative sensitivity of the value function with respect to that edge’s weight. If a small increase in  w_{ij}  would cause a large drop in future structural penalty (i.e.,  \partial V/\partial w_{ij}  is negative and large in magnitude), then a positive intervention is applied. The control is inversely proportional to the intervention cost  \gamma . In practice, the Cartographer’s digital twin (Chapter 8) solves this HJB numerically or via reinforcement learning to recommend daily team‑building actions that keep the colony’s knowledge graph near the ideal distributed form.

